A||N||10||Daleford||How do I test used rear struts?||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||12-24-2001||11:29 AM||||I have the rear stock struts out of my 86 chassis with the springs removed. Pulling the plunger out gives resistance. Pushing in it gives next to none.  Is this normal?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-24-2001||12:35 PM||||mostly look for "oil" on it when you pull it up..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Daleford||12-24-2001||01:07 PM||||No leaks anywhere, so I plan to use them.<BR> I would however like to hear views on that lack of resistance going in.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||12-24-2001||01:24 PM||||Lack of resistance "going in" is normal for the OEM struts.  <P>Although struts and shocks may appear to look and "test" OK, they do wear out over time.  Unless you're really strapped for cash, I would not go through the cost and effort to reinstall used (maybe original) struts, then deal with the wheel alignment issues. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||12-24-2001||01:35 PM||||At about 60.00 for Monroe struts why buy used. Mine on the cradle I have out are the same, they push in easily 170,000 KM tho!<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||12-24-2001||03:00 PM||||what if you get two new ones and one seems much easier to move in and out than the other. i called gabriel (the brand) and they said there could be differences but both should be in tolerance. since i cut the perches off for coilovers i can't take them back, but i am wondering about getting a third one and using which ever two feel most the same. would it be worth that trouble? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||12-24-2001||04:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroBUZZ:<BR><B>At about 60.00 for Monroe struts why buy used. Mine on the cradle I have out are the same, they push in easily 170,000 KM tho!<BR>Gary</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>$60 is <B>way</B> too much to pay for Monroe struts!  I can get them for $33.99 apiece, but even that is too much......Monroe just plain sucks (for lack of a better word).  <P>I bought a pair of Monroe shocks for the front end of my '88 GT and they were dead within 2 months.  The stuts are pretty weak too.  I would go with KYB shocks and stuts......in many cases they are cheaper than Monores or any other replacement.  I paid $16 each for the shocks and $52 each for the struts, so grand total was $136 (with shipping it was around $150).<P>As far as the question at hand.....if you push in on the strut rod and it stays down or is very slow in coming back up replace it.  It isn't worth the hassle of installing and re-aligning a strut that is dead or on it's last legs.<P>   <BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ToddAsh||12-24-2001||08:39 PM||||A better strut will have resistance in both directions.Even new Monroes have quite a bit of in and out pressure.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Daleford||12-24-2001||09:27 PM||||Mr. Fiero  I like those prices.  Where can i buy for that price?  Pep Boys or another chain? Merry Christmas<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||12-24-2001||09:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Daleford:<BR><B>Mr. Fiero  I like those prices.  Where can i buy for that price?  Pep Boys or another chain? Merry Christmas<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I bought mine online at <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com</A> <P>I'm not sure if they ship to Canada or not, but check them out and see.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierospeeder||12-24-2001||09:40 PM||||I would get brand new struts for a fiero.<BR>Unless your really broke.  <BR>the alignments gonna cost you, unless you got a lifetime align at firestone.<P><BR>I got a tbird turbo with auto struts.  these cost more then 160 bucks each.  I got two at the junkyard for 20 bucks each.  I push them down, and they uncompress.  No oil leak.  <BR>No alignment is necessary with my tbird, camber.  So im saving a lot of money, except the time it takes me to put them on my car.<P>||||reg||1
